@startuml "Flyweight - Book - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Flyweight — the same example written twice


package "book.wrong — not the pattern" {
  class "Character" as WC {
    - value : char
    - upperCase : boolean
    - line : Line
    - position : int
    + setLine(line)
    + setPosition(int)
  }
  class "BookFactory" as WF {
    - as : List<Character>
    + createCharacter(c, upper) : Character
  }
  WF ..> WC : "new, every time"
}

package "book.correct — the pattern" {
  class "Character" as CC <<ConcreteFlyweight>> {
    - value : char
    - upperCase : boolean
    + getValue() : char
  }
  class "CharacterFactory" as CF <<FlyweightFactory>> {
    - characters : Map<String, Character>
    + createCharacter(c, upper) : Character
    + createdCount() : int
  }
  class "Line" as CL {
    - chars : List<Character>
    + characterAt(position) : Character
  }
  CF ..> CC : "pools by (value, case)"
  CL o-- CC : "shared"
}

note bottom of WC
  <b>Two defects, and they interlock.</b>
  The factory never pools — and it could not,
  because position is stored <i>here</i>.
  Two occurrences of 'o' would fight
  over one field.
end note

note bottom of WF
  The pool field is
  <b>never read or written</b>.
end note

note bottom of CL
  Position is the <b>index in this list</b>.
  It needed no home at all.

  236 characters -> <b>29</b> objects.
end note

@enduml
